1
00:00:12,360 --> 00:00:15,236
Itadori, why is
his nose bleeding?

2
00:00:15,318 --> 00:00:15,610
I smashed in his face.

3
00:00:15,693 --> 00:00:16,527
But when?

4
00:00:16,610 --> 00:00:18,610
At the start of the fight.

5
00:00:18,693 --> 00:00:20,443
And did his hand touch you?

6
00:00:20,527 --> 00:00:21,568
Mm-hmm.

7
00:00:23,152 --> 00:00:24,544
My attacks aren't
going to work on him.

8
00:00:24,568 --> 00:00:26,277
Huh? Wait, what?

9
00:00:26,360 --> 00:00:28,401
But why not?

10
00:00:28,485 --> 00:00:30,610
I'll explain it later
while I'm lecturing you.

11
00:00:30,693 --> 00:00:31,527
It's either because, one:

12
00:00:31,610 --> 00:00:34,609
his technique doesn't
work on Itadori.

13
00:00:34,692 --> 00:00:37,317
Or two: there's some
reason he won't kill Itadori.

14
00:00:37,400 --> 00:00:39,859
Either way, it's good for us.

15
00:00:39,943 --> 00:00:42,609
However, I'll try to keep
him from moving around.

16
00:00:44,734 --> 00:00:46,901
Then, once we've
both got an opening,

17
00:00:46,984 --> 00:00:48,609
we'll shower him with blows.

18
00:00:49,526 --> 00:00:51,984
We'll exorcise this
one, here and now.

19
00:00:54,567 --> 00:00:55,608
Yeah!

20
00:01:03,192 --> 00:01:05,483
I'll keep an eye
on Yuuji Itadori,

21
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:10,192
while I start by taking out
the Seven to Three sorcerer.

22
00:01:29,233 --> 00:01:30,149
Hmmm.

23
00:01:30,233 --> 00:01:32,607
I thought that would
be a good one to use.

24
00:01:34,024 --> 00:01:35,732
But they both just dodged it

25
00:01:35,815 --> 00:01:38,398
and then, they started
shaving away the weaker ends.

26
00:01:39,814 --> 00:01:41,940
I guess it only
works on small fry.

27
00:01:42,023 --> 00:01:44,148
Time to stop!

28
00:01:44,232 --> 00:01:46,314
(roars)

29
00:01:46,397 --> 00:01:48,856
(attack grunt)

30
00:01:53,397 --> 00:01:55,481
Notice just before
he changes shape...

31
00:01:55,564 --> 00:01:56,981
He stores cursed energy.

32
00:01:57,065 --> 00:01:57,981
Right.

33
00:01:58,065 --> 00:01:58,814
(laughs)

34
00:01:58,898 --> 00:02:01,148
Even though I've
made myself smaller,

35
00:02:01,232 --> 00:02:02,664
there's still some
danger of Yuuji Itadori

36
00:02:02,688 --> 00:02:05,355
killing me in one blow.

37
00:02:05,438 --> 00:02:06,647
He really is my natural enemy.

38
00:02:06,730 --> 00:02:08,480
So I'll need to make him behave.

39
00:02:10,605 --> 00:02:11,980
(vomiting)

40
00:02:12,064 --> 00:02:12,772
Transfigured humans!

41
00:02:12,855 --> 00:02:16,189
He still had a
stockpile of them?

42
00:02:16,272 --> 00:02:18,105
Kill the short-haired brat, you!

43
00:02:25,687 --> 00:02:27,896
Look, he's running from them!

44
00:02:28,812 --> 00:02:30,979
I knew he couldn't kill humans!

45
00:02:31,063 --> 00:02:34,896
(attack chittering, gibberish)

46
00:02:45,646 --> 00:02:47,311
You wanna play?

47
00:02:49,686 --> 00:02:53,520
(attack chittering, gibberish)

48
00:02:56,478 --> 00:02:57,603
Please kill me.

49
00:02:57,686 --> 00:02:59,478
Please?

50
00:03:05,311 --> 00:03:07,770
Next I should have
him attack you, sorcerer.

51
00:03:07,853 --> 00:03:09,560
You think he'll cry then too?

52
00:03:09,644 --> 00:03:12,602
He's a foolish brat who
can't reconcile reality

53
00:03:12,685 --> 00:03:13,769
with his ideals.

54
00:03:13,852 --> 00:03:15,560
You're wrong about that.

55
00:03:15,644 --> 00:03:19,228
He's right in the process of
making that reconciliation.

56
00:03:19,310 --> 00:03:21,228
If you want to
know what I think...

57
00:03:21,310 --> 00:03:22,894
I'd say you're the fool.

58
00:03:26,894 --> 00:03:28,477
(surprised laugh)

59
00:03:28,560 --> 00:03:31,101
Did you kill those three?

60
00:03:34,351 --> 00:03:35,893
Damn, they know my tricks now!

61
00:03:35,976 --> 00:03:38,976
They know I change shape right
before the moment of impact.

62
00:03:42,559 --> 00:03:45,935
(agony yell)

63
00:03:49,726 --> 00:03:53,808
They're not giving me enough
time to create a substitute!

64
00:03:53,892 --> 00:03:55,267
Ahh!

65
00:03:55,350 --> 00:03:57,934
What fresh inspiration this is!

66
00:03:59,350 --> 00:04:01,433
Is this...

67
00:04:01,517 --> 00:04:02,517
Death?

68
00:04:06,517 --> 00:04:08,558
(building laughter)

69
00:04:10,391 --> 00:04:15,391
I bet I could do it now!

70
00:04:18,933 --> 00:04:20,432
Domain Expansion!

71
00:04:37,016 --> 00:04:39,431
Self-Embodiment of Perfection!

72
00:04:39,765 --> 00:04:41,556
No!

73
00:04:43,556 --> 00:04:45,973
Right now, I'm just so

74
00:04:47,556 --> 00:04:48,765
grateful to you.

75
00:04:49,765 --> 00:04:55,598
(opening theme music)

76
00:04:59,806 --> 00:05:03,223
"Jujutsu Kaisen"

77
00:06:19,886 --> 00:06:23,427
"Episode 13: Tomorrow"

78
00:06:23,511 --> 00:06:25,761
(punching efforts, grunting)

79
00:06:25,844 --> 00:06:27,302
Quit screwing around!

80
00:06:28,886 --> 00:06:31,968
Why'd he seal Nanami
inside and not me?

81
00:06:32,052 --> 00:06:33,219
What do I do?

82
00:06:33,301 --> 00:06:34,343
What can I do?

83
00:06:38,718 --> 00:06:41,052
Domain Expansion.

84
00:06:41,135 --> 00:06:44,219
Within an innate domain
constructed from cursed energy,

85
00:06:44,301 --> 00:06:45,760
the ultimate
technique becomes one

86
00:06:45,843 --> 00:06:47,885
that's guaranteed
to hit its target.

87
00:06:49,343 --> 00:06:51,759
It's the height of jujutsu
sorcery I could never reach.

88
00:06:53,675 --> 00:06:55,259
Most likely, his
cursed technique

89
00:06:55,342 --> 00:06:56,592
requires touching the target

90
00:06:56,675 --> 00:06:58,467
with his palm in its base state,

91
00:06:58,550 --> 00:07:01,300
in order to interfere
with the victim's soul.

92
00:07:01,383 --> 00:07:04,259
However, in a domain
that guarantees a hit,

93
00:07:04,342 --> 00:07:07,259
that would mean
that now, I'm literally...

94
00:07:07,342 --> 00:07:08,967
In the palm of his hand.

95
00:07:09,926 --> 00:07:10,842
Shit.

96
00:07:10,926 --> 00:07:14,466
Jujutsu sorcerers are shit.

97
00:07:14,549 --> 00:07:15,341
They have to be prepared

98
00:07:15,424 --> 00:07:17,633
to sacrifice their
lives for others,

99
00:07:17,716 --> 00:07:20,633
and occasionally force their
comrades to do so as well.

100
00:07:20,716 --> 00:07:22,133
That's why I quit.

101
00:07:23,091 --> 00:07:25,382
Though, ran away
is more like it.

102
00:07:26,591 --> 00:07:27,692
[Bakery Girl] You really like

103
00:07:27,716 --> 00:07:28,859
our ham and cheese, don't you?

104
00:07:28,883 --> 00:07:30,466
Huh?

105
00:07:30,549 --> 00:07:32,299
(laugh)

106
00:07:32,382 --> 00:07:34,299
You always order
the same sandwich.

107
00:07:34,382 --> 00:07:36,257
Oh, uh, yeah.

108
00:07:36,340 --> 00:07:39,507
They stopped selling it at
my local convenience store.

109
00:07:39,590 --> 00:07:42,298
Ours is probably better
than theirs anyway.

110
00:07:42,381 --> 00:07:44,507
Yeah, well you are a bakery.

111
00:07:44,590 --> 00:07:46,381
Hey, give us a little credit!

112
00:07:47,965 --> 00:07:49,632
See you next time!

113
00:07:53,216 --> 00:07:54,381
A fly head.

114
00:07:54,965 --> 00:07:56,840
Leaving it alone
won't hurt anything.

115
00:07:58,589 --> 00:08:00,672
It'd be a bigger
pain to deal with it

116
00:08:00,756 --> 00:08:02,356
and have her think I'm
some weird medium.

117
00:08:05,964 --> 00:08:08,131
Hello, everybody!

118
00:08:08,215 --> 00:08:08,881
Listen up!

119
00:08:08,964 --> 00:08:10,964
Make those sales!

120
00:08:11,048 --> 00:08:12,714
When people trust
us with their money,

121
00:08:12,797 --> 00:08:15,672
they're trusting
us with their lives.

122
00:08:15,756 --> 00:08:16,839
So it goes without saying

123
00:08:16,923 --> 00:08:19,048
that we have to balance
the pursuit of profit

124
00:08:19,131 --> 00:08:20,547
against the risks.

125
00:08:20,630 --> 00:08:23,172
There's no need to do
anything special at the start.

126
00:08:23,255 --> 00:08:25,379
Just be sincere
with the clients.

127
00:08:25,463 --> 00:08:26,379
Mm-hmm.

128
00:08:26,463 --> 00:08:28,338
Try never to forget that.

129
00:08:28,421 --> 00:08:28,922
[New Guy] Right!

130
00:08:29,005 --> 00:08:31,214
Nanami...

131
00:08:31,296 --> 00:08:33,172
Don't be so damned
serious all the time,

132
00:08:33,255 --> 00:08:34,963
you're freaking out the virgin.

133
00:08:35,047 --> 00:08:38,088
New boy, what you
need to think about first

134
00:08:38,172 --> 00:08:39,088
is the company's profits!

135
00:08:39,172 --> 00:08:41,755
If we don't profit then
neither does the client!

136
00:08:41,838 --> 00:08:45,171
Even when we con them
into buying shit stocks

137
00:08:45,254 --> 00:08:46,171
with no growth potential?

138
00:08:46,254 --> 00:08:47,171
Of course!

139
00:08:47,254 --> 00:08:48,171
It's a well-deserved payment

140
00:08:48,254 --> 00:08:50,087
given the fact that
we spend our days

141
00:08:50,171 --> 00:08:52,087
staring at the markets
around the clock!

142
00:08:52,171 --> 00:08:54,545
Nanami, this is your
second year, right?

143
00:08:54,629 --> 00:08:57,087
You're clever, let
yourself run wild, okay!

144
00:08:57,171 --> 00:08:59,545
I expect great things from you!

145
00:08:59,629 --> 00:09:01,879
I'm a person who's never
gotten the concept of

146
00:09:01,962 --> 00:09:05,586
"reason for living" or
"something worth doing."

147
00:09:05,669 --> 00:09:07,377
I figure I'll just
earn enough money

148
00:09:07,461 --> 00:09:08,253
by the time I'm 30 or 40,

149
00:09:08,336 --> 00:09:09,961
to enjoy the rest
of my aimless life

150
00:09:10,045 --> 00:09:13,753
in some country with
a low cost of living.

151
00:09:13,836 --> 00:09:16,586
It's been four years
since I left the school.

152
00:09:16,669 --> 00:09:18,377
Now, whether I'm
awake or asleep,

153
00:09:18,461 --> 00:09:19,541
all I think about is money.

154
00:09:19,586 --> 00:09:22,753
Curses and other people
have nothing to do with me,

155
00:09:22,836 --> 00:09:24,586
as long I have money.

156
00:09:24,669 --> 00:09:25,669
Money.

157
00:09:26,669 --> 00:09:27,960
Money.

158
00:09:28,044 --> 00:09:29,085
Money.

159
00:09:30,668 --> 00:09:31,668
Money, money.

160
00:09:32,668 --> 00:09:34,960
As long as I have money.

161
00:09:35,044 --> 00:09:36,668
Are you all right?

162
00:09:37,668 --> 00:09:39,061
I mean are you
getting enough sleep?

163
00:09:39,085 --> 00:09:39,960
What about you?

164
00:09:40,044 --> 00:09:42,585
You look like you've
been carrying around

165
00:09:42,668 --> 00:09:44,002
some serious stress.

166
00:09:44,085 --> 00:09:46,502
Ha, you can tell that huh?

167
00:09:46,585 --> 00:09:50,210
Lately I feel like there's
this weight on my shoulder.

168
00:09:50,292 --> 00:09:52,126
I haven't been
sleeping well, either.

169
00:09:53,542 --> 00:09:54,685
[Nanami] Essentially my job--

170
00:09:54,709 --> 00:09:55,792
Hm?

171
00:09:55,876 --> 00:09:58,001
Is to take money
from wealthy people,

172
00:09:58,084 --> 00:10:01,792
and use it to make those
people even more wealthy.

173
00:10:01,876 --> 00:10:03,036
That's pretty much all it is.

174
00:10:03,084 --> 00:10:06,959
Frankly no one would even
mind if I were to just vanish.

175
00:10:07,043 --> 00:10:08,417
But people who wanted bread

176
00:10:08,501 --> 00:10:11,417
would definitely mind
if their bakery was gone.

177
00:10:11,501 --> 00:10:13,250
Yet for some reason, my job,

178
00:10:13,333 --> 00:10:17,167
which exists completely outside
of that natural human cycle,

179
00:10:17,250 --> 00:10:18,666
pays better money.

180
00:10:18,750 --> 00:10:20,059
When you think
about it logically,

181
00:10:20,083 --> 00:10:22,500
it really doesn't
make any sense at all.

182
00:10:23,708 --> 00:10:24,958
Are you bragging?

183
00:10:25,042 --> 00:10:26,042
No, I'm not.

184
00:10:26,083 --> 00:10:27,000
(cursed fly-buzzing laugh)

185
00:10:27,083 --> 00:10:28,167
(laugh)

186
00:10:28,250 --> 00:10:31,167
Sorry. That was a bit
complicated for me to follow!

187
00:10:31,250 --> 00:10:33,000
Could you take a
step forward, please?

188
00:10:35,916 --> 00:10:36,916
Uhh.

189
00:10:39,124 --> 00:10:40,124
Hm?

190
00:10:40,166 --> 00:10:41,665
How does your shoulder feel now?

191
00:10:41,749 --> 00:10:42,665
Huh?

192
00:10:42,749 --> 00:10:44,665
Oh! Wow, it's lighter!

193
00:10:44,749 --> 00:10:45,749
It's all better!

194
00:10:45,832 --> 00:10:48,665
If it still feels off you
should go see a doctor.

195
00:10:48,749 --> 00:10:49,790
Goodbye.

196
00:10:51,124 --> 00:10:52,290
Ahh!

197
00:10:52,373 --> 00:10:54,499
Oh, uh wait!

198
00:10:54,582 --> 00:10:55,041
Hold on!

199
00:10:55,124 --> 00:10:56,915
Mister?

200
00:10:59,372 --> 00:11:00,748
Hey, thank you!

201
00:11:01,915 --> 00:11:03,998
I hope we see you again soon!

202
00:11:04,081 --> 00:11:05,456
Thank you...

203
00:11:05,539 --> 00:11:06,664
[Bakery Girl] Hey!

204
00:11:06,748 --> 00:11:08,040
Did you hear me?

205
00:11:08,123 --> 00:11:11,331
Thanks, and please
come back again soon!

206
00:11:11,414 --> 00:11:13,224
[Nanami] I always thought I
was a person with no concept

207
00:11:13,248 --> 00:11:15,414
of a "reason for living."

208
00:11:17,789 --> 00:11:19,039
Hello, it's Nanami.

209
00:11:19,122 --> 00:11:20,788
I need to talk to you.

210
00:11:22,371 --> 00:11:24,131
Yes, I want to stop by
Jujutsu Tech tomorrow.

211
00:11:26,122 --> 00:11:27,164
Why are you laughing?

212
00:11:31,788 --> 00:11:33,080
Idle Transfiguration.

213
00:11:33,164 --> 00:11:35,413
I'm so grateful to you.

214
00:11:39,247 --> 00:11:41,829
Save your gratitude.

215
00:11:47,621 --> 00:11:50,829
I've already received more
than enough of that from others.

216
00:11:51,246 --> 00:11:54,287
I've no regrets.

217
00:11:54,370 --> 00:11:55,287
(snickers)

218
00:11:55,370 --> 00:11:57,996
(glass breaks)

219
00:11:59,662 --> 00:12:02,621
(surprised gasps)

220
00:12:03,828 --> 00:12:04,828
(short attack roar)

221
00:12:08,286 --> 00:12:09,995
How was he able to get in?

222
00:12:10,995 --> 00:12:11,995
That's it.

223
00:12:12,078 --> 00:12:14,912
The more resistant the
inside of the barrier is,

224
00:12:14,995 --> 00:12:17,578
the weaker it is to
attacks from outside.

225
00:12:17,661 --> 00:12:19,953
Domains are barriers meant
for trapping something inside,

226
00:12:20,037 --> 00:12:23,204
so they're actually
easy to invade,

227
00:12:24,037 --> 00:12:26,994
because there's no
merit in doing so.

228
00:12:29,827 --> 00:12:32,577
That's even more true with
Domains like Infinite Void

229
00:12:32,660 --> 00:12:34,619
and Self-Embodiment
of Perfection,

230
00:12:34,702 --> 00:12:37,911
which guarantee victory once
they've ensnared their target.

231
00:12:40,410 --> 00:12:43,119
However, inside Itadori,

232
00:12:43,203 --> 00:12:45,077
there lies something
that must not be touched!

233
00:12:52,243 --> 00:12:53,451
I warned you,

234
00:12:56,868 --> 00:12:58,868
there'd be no second time.

235
00:13:03,035 --> 00:13:03,868
(shock gasps)

236
00:13:03,951 --> 00:13:05,219
[Nanami] There is
no one in this world

237
00:13:05,243 --> 00:13:07,160
more proud and conceited.

238
00:13:07,243 --> 00:13:11,242
He lives guided by only his
own pleasure and displeasure.

239
00:13:12,366 --> 00:13:17,492
Whether you die or you
die doesn't matter to me.

240
00:13:20,075 --> 00:13:21,117
Aside from him.

241
00:13:22,742 --> 00:13:24,492
I truly don't care.

242
00:13:43,074 --> 00:13:45,324
(pain moan)

243
00:13:47,449 --> 00:13:48,949
"JUJUTSU KAISEN"

244
00:13:53,074 --> 00:13:54,324
"JUJUTSU KAISEN"

245
00:14:00,364 --> 00:14:02,406
(pain moan)

246
00:14:02,490 --> 00:14:04,323
What just happened?

247
00:14:07,948 --> 00:14:09,281
(determined grunt)

248
00:14:09,364 --> 00:14:11,656
(charge yell)

249
00:14:11,740 --> 00:14:12,990
I'll kill you!

250
00:14:14,115 --> 00:14:17,405
Domain Expansion really
burns cursed energy.

251
00:14:17,489 --> 00:14:20,864
It truly is a trump
card, a final technique.

252
00:14:20,947 --> 00:14:22,072
And that damn Sukuna just...

253
00:14:22,156 --> 00:14:24,864
But this is the critical moment!

254
00:14:24,947 --> 00:14:25,572
Squeeze it out!

255
00:14:25,655 --> 00:14:28,405
The last of my cursed energy!

256
00:14:28,489 --> 00:14:31,655
(monster roar)

257
00:14:31,739 --> 00:14:33,405
The target's huge.

258
00:14:33,489 --> 00:14:35,114
The flow of cursed
energy is calm.

259
00:14:36,780 --> 00:14:37,363
There are no options.

260
00:14:37,447 --> 00:14:39,905
I know I can land my attack.

261
00:14:39,988 --> 00:14:41,404
This is my last chance!

262
00:14:43,362 --> 00:14:45,238
I don't need any more tactics!

263
00:14:52,321 --> 00:14:53,321
Divergent Fist!

264
00:15:03,987 --> 00:15:04,904
Huh?

265
00:15:04,987 --> 00:15:05,904
Huh!

266
00:15:05,987 --> 00:15:07,196
What's this lack of feedback?

267
00:15:09,987 --> 00:15:11,029
Bye-bye!

268
00:15:11,778 --> 00:15:13,070
Hold it!

269
00:15:13,154 --> 00:15:14,154
This was fun!

270
00:15:19,570 --> 00:15:20,612
Shit.

271
00:15:22,196 --> 00:15:23,112
Ino!

272
00:15:23,196 --> 00:15:25,402
The core has escaped
back into the sewers.

273
00:15:26,402 --> 00:15:27,777
Yeah.

274
00:15:27,861 --> 00:15:28,944
Please scour everything

275
00:15:29,028 --> 00:15:30,668
from my current
location to the southeast.

276
00:15:32,028 --> 00:15:34,486
Even you could
exorcise him right now.

277
00:15:34,569 --> 00:15:36,486
We need to go after him and...

278
00:15:36,569 --> 00:15:37,611
Huh?

279
00:15:38,028 --> 00:15:39,319
Itadori!

280
00:15:39,402 --> 00:15:41,153
Come on body, move!

281
00:15:41,236 --> 00:15:44,777
You're going to kill
that thing, aren't you?

282
00:15:44,861 --> 00:15:45,527
You said you were gonna

283
00:15:45,611 --> 00:15:48,276
-crush him into a pulp!
-Itadori!

284
00:15:48,359 --> 00:15:49,401
Itadori!

285
00:15:53,443 --> 00:15:57,860
(groan into panting grunt)

286
00:16:04,068 --> 00:16:06,235
(giggling)

287
00:16:12,234 --> 00:16:16,317
So that was the King of
Curses, Ryoumen Sukuna.

288
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:18,293
He should have less total
cursed energy than Jougo

289
00:16:18,317 --> 00:16:22,151
at this point in
time, and yet...

290
00:16:22,234 --> 00:16:23,984
That presence!

291
00:16:24,067 --> 00:16:27,151
His soul's on a different level.

292
00:16:27,234 --> 00:16:28,984
I'm certain of it.

293
00:16:29,067 --> 00:16:30,774
Even if we're all wiped out,

294
00:16:30,858 --> 00:16:32,357
as long as Sukuna
is resurrected,

295
00:16:32,441 --> 00:16:33,561
the age of curses will come.

296
00:16:35,608 --> 00:16:37,357
But damn, this still sucks.

297
00:16:37,441 --> 00:16:41,941
Right now, I want nothing
more than to kill Yuuji Itadori!

298
00:16:47,274 --> 00:16:50,858
Arrgghh, it's so frustrating!

299
00:16:50,941 --> 00:16:53,191
But whatever, because,

300
00:16:53,273 --> 00:16:55,815
unlike his body I can
keep killing his soul

301
00:16:55,899 --> 00:16:57,273
over and over again.

302
00:16:59,107 --> 00:17:02,565
So next time what would
be a fun way to kill it?

303
00:17:02,648 --> 00:17:06,356
(malicious giggle)

304
00:17:06,440 --> 00:17:08,690
[Nanami] You were
told to rest, weren't you?

305
00:17:10,273 --> 00:17:12,024
[Itadori] Is this my lecture?

306
00:17:12,107 --> 00:17:14,191
I have no lecture
at all to give you.

307
00:17:14,273 --> 00:17:16,606
You're the one
who saved my life.

308
00:17:16,689 --> 00:17:18,023
I saved you?

309
00:17:18,106 --> 00:17:20,023
That patchwork's
cursed technique

310
00:17:20,106 --> 00:17:22,190
is interfering with the soul.

311
00:17:22,314 --> 00:17:25,064
Because you invaded
his Expansion Domain,

312
00:17:25,148 --> 00:17:27,439
he wound up inadvertently
touching Sukuna's soul.

313
00:17:27,522 --> 00:17:30,272
I was saved because of that.

314
00:17:30,355 --> 00:17:33,355
But, I never swapped
out with Sukuna.

315
00:17:34,606 --> 00:17:37,855
[Nanami] Sukuna never came out.

316
00:17:37,938 --> 00:17:39,313
Our opponent went in.

317
00:17:40,563 --> 00:17:43,605
Then it wasn't me who saved you.

318
00:17:43,688 --> 00:17:45,354
It was just Sukuna's whim.

319
00:17:46,480 --> 00:17:49,563
Nanami, I killed a person today.

320
00:17:51,147 --> 00:17:52,063
People die.

321
00:17:52,147 --> 00:17:53,396
There's no stopping that.

322
00:17:53,480 --> 00:17:55,360
So I wanted them to at
least have proper deaths.

323
00:17:57,147 --> 00:17:58,605
That's what I thought.

324
00:17:58,688 --> 00:18:00,229
So I was always thinking about

325
00:18:00,312 --> 00:18:02,645
how I could keep that
trigger from being pulled.

326
00:18:02,729 --> 00:18:06,104
But, after pulling
that trigger myself,

327
00:18:06,188 --> 00:18:07,896
I don't understand anymore!

328
00:18:07,979 --> 00:18:08,729
What is a proper death?

329
00:18:08,812 --> 00:18:10,395
I don't know
what that is, either.

330
00:18:11,562 --> 00:18:14,729
Even if all good people
properly died in peace,

331
00:18:14,812 --> 00:18:17,104
and all evil people
were punished in death,

332
00:18:17,188 --> 00:18:18,621
the problem would be that
most people in this world

333
00:18:18,645 --> 00:18:21,729
are neither all
good nor all evil.

334
00:18:21,812 --> 00:18:23,537
Death is the final
destination for all of us,

335
00:18:23,561 --> 00:18:26,269
but no one dies the same death.

336
00:18:26,352 --> 00:18:28,103
Guiding all of them
to their proper end

337
00:18:28,187 --> 00:18:29,644
would be quite arduous.

338
00:18:29,728 --> 00:18:31,394
I personally wouldn't
recommend it.

339
00:18:32,728 --> 00:18:33,478
I know you won't listen.

340
00:18:33,561 --> 00:18:36,020
You'll still try won't you?

341
00:18:37,352 --> 00:18:39,936
I hope you don't get
killed in the process.

342
00:18:40,020 --> 00:18:43,103
And, just as I would've died
today if you hadn't been there,

343
00:18:43,187 --> 00:18:45,894
you'll see that there are plenty
of other people yet to come

344
00:18:45,977 --> 00:18:47,685
who are going to need you too.

345
00:18:47,768 --> 00:18:50,435
Just remember, Itadori,
you're a jujutsu sorcerer now.

346
00:18:52,602 --> 00:18:56,310
(overwhelmed breath)

347
00:18:56,393 --> 00:18:58,144
The survey is
completely anonymous

348
00:18:58,227 --> 00:18:59,685
so please don't
write your names.

349
00:18:59,768 --> 00:19:01,560
When you're done
put them in this box.

350
00:19:01,643 --> 00:19:02,643
"Survey on Bullying"

351
00:19:03,685 --> 00:19:07,434
(mellow instrumental music)

352
00:19:23,226 --> 00:19:25,143
It was you wasn't it, Itou?

353
00:19:25,226 --> 00:19:27,476
You gave Yoshino
the scars, right?

354
00:19:28,809 --> 00:19:30,017
(sneering)

355
00:19:30,100 --> 00:19:31,784
That's rich, coming
from the so-called teacher

356
00:19:31,808 --> 00:19:34,391
who was too scared to do
anything about it at the time.

357
00:19:34,475 --> 00:19:38,184
Anyway he quit school
and moved away, didn't he?

358
00:19:38,266 --> 00:19:40,349
So who cares?

359
00:19:40,433 --> 00:19:41,975
'N what about me?

360
00:19:42,058 --> 00:19:44,725
I've barely been able to move
my left arm since that day!

361
00:19:44,808 --> 00:19:47,391
All we're concerned with
here and now are your crimes.

362
00:19:47,475 --> 00:19:49,017
Use your own time to reflect

363
00:19:49,100 --> 00:19:51,017
on the punishment
you brought on yourself.

364
00:19:51,100 --> 00:19:52,974
And where's your punishment?

365
00:19:53,057 --> 00:19:54,724
Mine is yet to come.

366
00:19:54,807 --> 00:19:57,932
First I have to look at the
things to which I was blind.

367
00:19:58,682 --> 00:20:02,183
Both you, and I,

368
00:20:02,265 --> 00:20:04,724
will have to live with the
crime of killing Yoshino's heart

369
00:20:04,807 --> 00:20:06,724
for the rest of our lives.

370
00:20:06,807 --> 00:20:09,557
I'll be watching you, Itou.

371
00:20:12,307 --> 00:20:15,389
♪ But I'll survive ♪

372
00:20:15,473 --> 00:20:18,848
I don't really understand
what a proper death is.

373
00:20:18,931 --> 00:20:19,931
So for now,

374
00:20:21,848 --> 00:20:23,306
until I do understand,

375
00:20:26,473 --> 00:20:27,931
until I kill him,

376
00:20:39,305 --> 00:20:40,680
I will not

377
00:20:43,472 --> 00:20:44,472
lose again.

378
00:20:47,097 --> 00:20:52,139
(ending theme music

379
00:22:14,885 --> 00:22:17,135
[In Unison] Juju Stroll!

380
00:22:17,218 --> 00:22:18,218
[Toge] Tuna.

381
00:22:21,426 --> 00:22:22,426
Is it ready yet?

382
00:22:23,426 --> 00:22:24,426
Salmon, salmon.

383
00:22:29,967 --> 00:22:31,134
Huh?

384
00:22:31,217 --> 00:22:32,675
These are some
really good meatballs.

385
00:22:32,758 --> 00:22:33,675
So who made 'em?

386
00:22:33,758 --> 00:22:35,675
Oh, I did.

387
00:22:35,758 --> 00:22:37,341
They're easy to make.

388
00:22:37,425 --> 00:22:40,717
"Put all the ingredients in.
Use twice as much ginger."

389
00:22:40,800 --> 00:22:44,176
"Mix together
well and knead it."

390
00:22:44,258 --> 00:22:47,758
"Shape with spoons
and toss into the pot."

391
00:22:47,842 --> 00:22:49,134
"Ingredients"

392
00:22:49,217 --> 00:22:51,340
"Ground chicken, finely
chopped green onions,

393
00:22:51,424 --> 00:22:54,507
"ginger paste, egg
yolks, salt and pepper"

394
00:22:54,591 --> 00:22:55,799
Bonito flakes.

395
00:22:57,257 --> 00:22:59,549
[Nobara] So you like to
cook for yourself, huh?

396
00:22:59,632 --> 00:23:00,650
Not too surprising, actually.

397
00:23:00,674 --> 00:23:04,299
Well, Itadori taught
me how to make 'em.

398
00:23:05,091 --> 00:23:07,841
(Panda chewing)

399
00:23:14,256 --> 00:23:16,048
That's sad.

400
00:23:17,090 --> 00:23:19,548
Itadori's legacy is a meatball.

401
00:23:19,631 --> 00:23:21,256
[Maki] I don't
think that's right.

402
00:23:22,256 --> 00:23:24,756
(sneezing)

403
00:23:24,840 --> 00:23:26,715
These are some
really good meatballs.

404
00:23:26,798 --> 00:23:29,673
Yeah, and guess what,
they're super easy to make.

405
00:23:31,631 --> 00:23:32,631
Even Fushiguro can do it.

406
00:23:32,673 --> 00:23:33,715
I taught him how.

407
00:23:38,006 --> 00:23:40,505
I can't wait to see
those two again.

408
00:23:45,047 --> 00:23:47,714
(upbeat electronic music)

409
00:23:50,881 --> 00:23:53,422
"Episode 14: Kyoto Sister
School Exchange Event

410
00:23:53,505 --> 00:23:54,672
"- Group Battle"

